MVP Specification
Virtual World Platform v0.1
Version: 1.0
Status: Pre-Production
Target Platform: Windows Desktop
Engine: Unity 6
Backend: Nakama + PostgreSQL
Purpose: Validate the core social virtual world experience before introducing economies, marketplaces, creator systems, age progression, and teen environments.

Executive Summary
The MVP exists to answer a single question:

Will users enjoy entering a persistent virtual social world, customising their avatar, decorating their personal space, and interacting with other users?

The MVP is not intended to launch the complete vision of the platform.

The objective is to validate:

Avatar creation
Multiplayer networking
Social interaction
Virtual housing
Data persistence
User retention
before investing in:

Virtual economy
Marketplace
Creator monetisation
Teen environment
Mobile support
Voice communication
Success Criteria
Technical Goals
Support 50 concurrent users
Stable multiplayer sessions
Persistent user accounts
Persistent housing layouts
Reliable chat functionality
User Experience Goals
Users should:

Create an avatar
Explore the virtual world
Socialise with others
Decorate their apartment
Return to the platform repeatedly
Architectural Goals
The MVP architecture must support future implementation of:

Age Progression System (APS)
Teen Environment
Creator Marketplace
Mobile Applications
Virtual Economy
